<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR mostly lower in liquid market.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR mostly lower in liquid market.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) dropped in most maturities on Friday due to little demand for pesos in a liquid market, traders said.</p>
<p>However, the two, six and 12-month rates were unchanged.</p>
<p>The ample peso liquidity prodded banks into adjusting their swap rates at the PHIBOR market.</p>
<p>PHIBOR represents rates at which banks are willing to swap their pesos for dollars.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  NOV 15		 NOV 14</p>
<p>    1 W		11  5/8		 11  3/4</p>
<p>    2 W		11  5/8		 11  3/4</p>
<p>    1 M		11 11/16		11  3/4</p>
<p>    2 M		11 11/16		11 11/16</p>
<p>    3 M		11 11/16		11  3/4</p>
<p>    6 M		11  7/8		 11  7/8</p>
<p>    12M		11  7/8		 11  7/8</p>
<p>    VAL		18-Nov		  15-Nov</p>
<p>--LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
